#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:6
msgid "Cash register"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:8
msgid "The **Cash register** (*Házipénztár*) turns an Odoo cash journal into a Hungarian strict-accountability (*szigorú számadás*) cash book. It adds gap-free numbered cash-in and cash-out vouchers, serially numbered cash-book statements (*kivonat*), an amount spelled out in words on every voucher, and protection against back-dating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:13
msgid "The module builds on standard Odoo :ref:`cash journals <accounting/journals/cash>` and the :guilabel:`Accounting Dashboard`; it does not replace them, it extends them with the controls a serially-numbered, audit-proof cash book requires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:18
msgid "Key features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:20
msgid "**Four no-gap numbering sequences per cash journal**: one for the journal entries, one for the cash-book statements (``STAT``), and one each for cash-in (``BEF``) and cash-out (``KIF``) vouchers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:23
msgid "**Numbered cash vouchers**: every posted cash-in or cash-out movement receives a continuous, per-year number and an amount written out in words (*betűs összeg*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:25
msgid "**Cash-book statements**: a cash-book page can be opened and later confirmed (locked); the ``STAT`` number is assigned only on confirmation, so an open page never burns a number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:27
msgid "**Back-dating protection**: a voucher cannot be dated earlier than the last already-numbered voucher, keeping the numbering and the dates monotonic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:29
msgid "**Cash count on closing**: the drawer can be counted by denomination and closed with an automatic discrepancy check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register.rst:43
msgid "The Cash register is an *eYssen* extension for Hungarian localization. Once the cash journals are configured, day-to-day operations (vouchers, statements, closing) are handled from the :guilabel:`Accounting Dashboard`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:6
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/egypt.rst:8
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/india.rst:8
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/united_arab_emirates.rst:8
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:8
msgid "Navigate to :menuselection:`Apps`, search for **Cash Register**, and click :guilabel:`Install`. The module depends on :guilabel:`Accounting`; on a Hungarian localization database it is usually installed together with the localization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:13
msgid "Configuring the numbering sequences is restricted to users in the :guilabel:`Billing Administrator` (*Főkönyvelő*) group. Cashiers do not need access to the configuration to record vouchers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:18
msgid "Set up a cash journal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:20
msgid "Each physical cash desk is a separate cash journal, one per currency (for example *Cash HUF*, *Cash EUR*). To create one, go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Journals`, click :guilabel:`New`, and set the :guilabel:`Type` to :guilabel:`Cash`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:24
msgid "On a cash journal, the :guilabel:`Journal Entries` tab shows an extra **Cash Book Sequences** group where the four numbering sequences and the auto-statement option are assigned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:38
msgid "Numbering sequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:40
msgid "The module ships four ready-made :guilabel:`No gap` sequences that you assign on each cash journal. A *no-gap* sequence guarantees a continuous, audit-proof numbering as required by Hungarian strict accountability, and each sequence restarts every year."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:48
msgid "Field"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:49
msgid "Prefix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:50
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/nav_online_invoice.rst:133
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:51
msgid ":guilabel:`Journal Sequence`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:52
msgid "``NAPLO/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:53
msgid "Numbers the journal entries of this cash journal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:54
msgid ":guilabel:`Statement Sequence`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:55
msgid "``STAT/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:56
msgid "Assigned to each cash-book statement when it is confirmed (*kivonat sorszám*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:57
msgid ":guilabel:`Cash-in Sequence`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:58
msgid "``BEF/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:59
msgid "Numbers inbound cash vouchers (*befizetés sorszám*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:60
msgid ":guilabel:`Cash-out Sequence`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:61
msgid "``KIF/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:62
msgid "Numbers outbound cash vouchers (*kifizetés sorszám*)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:65
msgid "You can assign the **same** sequence to :guilabel:`Cash-in Sequence` and :guilabel:`Cash-out Sequence` to keep a single running number across both directions, or assign **two different** sequences to number each direction separately. This choice also widens or narrows the scope of the back-dating check (see :ref:`cash_register/back-dating`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:70
msgid "To create your own sequences, duplicate the supplied templates in :menuselection:`Settings --> Technical --> Sequences & Identifiers --> Sequences`, keep the :guilabel:`Implementation` set to :guilabel:`No gap`, and select them on the journal. The running number is never reset by a module upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:76
msgid "Auto statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:78
msgid "Enable :guilabel:`Auto Statement` on the journal so that posting a cash voucher automatically opens or attaches a cash-book statement when none is open. Leave it disabled to open the cash-book pages manually."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:85
msgid "Back-dating protection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:87
msgid "By default the cash book is protected against back-dating: a voucher cannot be posted with a date earlier than the last already-numbered voucher in its numbering scope. This keeps the numbering and the dates monotonic, as required for a strict-accountability cash book."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/configuration.rst:91
msgid "An administrator can lift this restriction by setting the system parameter ``eyssen_cashregister.override_sequence_date_constraint`` to ``1`` in :menuselection:`Settings --> Technical --> System Parameters`. The default value ``0`` keeps the protection active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:3
msgid "Operations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:5
msgid "Day-to-day cash handling is done from the :guilabel:`Accounting Dashboard`. On a cash journal card, the cash-register actions are available next to the standard buttons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:18
msgid "Record a cash-in or cash-out voucher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:20
msgid "On the cash journal card, click :guilabel:`New Cash-in` for money received, or :guilabel:`New Cash-out` for money paid out. A cash voucher form opens with the journal and the direction already filled in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:23
msgid "Select the :guilabel:`Customer` or :guilabel:`Vendor` and enter the :guilabel:`Amount`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:24
msgid "Fill in the cash-specific fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:26
msgid ":guilabel:`Pretense` (*Jogcím*): the reason for the cash movement. It is editable only while the voucher is a draft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:28
msgid ":guilabel:`Date`: the voucher date. It may not be earlier than the last numbered voucher (see :ref:`cash_register/back-dating`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:31
msgid "Confirm the voucher. On posting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:33
msgid "It receives the next gap-free number from the journal's :guilabel:`Cash-in Sequence` or :guilabel:`Cash-out Sequence` (for example ``BEF/2026/00012`` or ``KIF/2026/00007``), shown in :guilabel:`Voucher Number`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:36
msgid "The :guilabel:`Amount in Words` (*betűs összeg*) is filled in automatically for the printed voucher."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:49
msgid "A draft voucher that is cancelled never consumes a number, so the numbering stays gap-free. Once a voucher carries a number it can no longer be deleted, which preserves the audit trail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:53
msgid "Cash-book statements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:55
msgid "A cash-book statement (*pénztárkönyv / kivonat*) is a numbered page that groups a period's cash movements. A statement is **Open** while it accepts entries and **Confirmed** once it is closed and locked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:70
msgid "Confirm a cash book"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:72
msgid "When a cash-book page is complete, select it in the statement list and choose :menuselection:`Action --> Confirm cash-book`. On confirmation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:75
msgid "The statement receives the next gap-free :guilabel:`STAT Number` from the journal's :guilabel:`Statement Sequence` (for example ``STAT/2026/00013``). Because the number is assigned only on confirmation, an open page never burns a ``STAT`` number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:78
msgid "The :guilabel:`Cash-book State` changes to :guilabel:`Confirmed`, and the page and its number can no longer be altered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:82
msgid "Reopen a cash book"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:84
msgid "A confirmed cash book can be reopened with :menuselection:`Action --> Reopen cash-book`. This action is restricted to the :guilabel:`Billing Administrator` (*Főkönyvelő*) group. Reopening keeps the existing ``STAT`` number — a cash book is never re-numbered — and is recorded in the chatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:89
msgid "Close and count the cash drawer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:91
msgid "To reconcile the physical cash on hand, click :guilabel:`Close Cash Register` on the cash journal card. Count the drawer by denomination; the system compares the counted amount with the journal balance and reports any discrepancy. A controller can review and approve a discrepancy before the count is closed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:106
msgid "Fill in the number of coins and bills per :guilabel:`Denomination`; the :guilabel:`Counted Balance` and the :guilabel:`Discrepancy` against the :guilabel:`Cash Balance in Journal` are computed as you type. If there is no difference, click :guilabel:`Close`. If there is one, enter the :guilabel:`Reason for Discrepancy`, appoint a :guilabel:`Controller` (it cannot be yourself) and click :guilabel:`Close with Discrepancy`; the closure then waits for that controller's approval. :guilabel:`Print` produces the cash count sheet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/cash_register/operations.rst:113
msgid "Past closures are listed under :menuselection:`Accounting --> Reporting --> Cash Register Closures`, where they can be filtered by state (:guilabel:`Draft`, :guilabel:`Waiting for Approval`, :guilabel:`Closed`) and grouped by cash register, user or controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/foreign_currency.rst:3
msgid "Manage a bank account in a foreign currency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/bank/foreign_currency.rst:5
msgid "In Odoo, every transaction is recorded in the default currency of the company, and reports are all based on that default currency. When you have a bank account in a foreign currency, for every transaction, Odoo stores two values:"
msgstr ""

