#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:129
msgid ":guilabel:`Collection fee (B2B)`: optionally add a fixed collection fee, applied only to company (business) customers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:132
msgid "The block is only shown on levels whose :guilabel:`Show Late-payment Interest` option is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:135
msgid "These amounts are **display-only**. They are computed and shown on the reminder for information, but the application **never** creates a journal entry — no interest or fee is posted to accounting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:148
msgid "Invoices treated as paid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:150
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings` and, in the :guilabel:`Customer Invoices` section, set :guilabel:`Invoices treated as paid`. The choice applies to the daily automatic reminders **and** to every manual send (from a customer, a customer list, or the invoices list)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:155
msgid ":guilabel:`Fully Paid` (default): only fully paid invoices are skipped. Invoices in :guilabel:`In Payment` — a payment was registered but has not yet been matched on the bank statement — are still included, even when an open amount remains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:159
msgid ":guilabel:`Fully Paid and In Payment`: also skip invoices in :guilabel:`In Payment`. Use this when a registered payment should not trigger a reminder while it waits for bank matching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:163
msgid "Reversed invoices are always skipped. Unpaid and partially paid invoices are always included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:176
msgid "Follow-up process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:179
msgid "Reconcile all bank transactions before starting the follow-up process to avoid sending reminders for invoices that have already been paid. To also skip invoices that are still :guilabel:`In Payment` while they wait for bank matching, set :guilabel:`Invoices treated as paid` to :guilabel:`Fully Paid and In Payment` (see :ref:`accounting/follow_up/settled`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:188
msgid "Follow-ups for one customer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:190
msgid "For a detailed overview of a customer's follow-up status, go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Customers --> Customers`, open the customer's form, and click the :guilabel:`Payment Follow-up` tab. The tab shows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:194
msgid ":guilabel:`Follow-up Status`: :guilabel:`No Action Needed`, :guilabel:`In Need of Action`, or :guilabel:`With Overdue Invoices`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:196
msgid ":guilabel:`Next Follow-up Date`: the throttle date before which the customer will not be dunned again; set automatically after a reminder is sent and manually adjustable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:198
msgid ":guilabel:`Follow-up Responsible`: the user who handles the follow-up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:199
msgid ":guilabel:`Total Overdue` and :guilabel:`Total Due`: the customer's overdue and total open receivable amounts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:209
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Send Reminder` to open the review window, adjust the :guilabel:`Level` if needed, and click :guilabel:`Send`. The reminder covers the customer's **full overdue statement**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:213
msgid "The contact information on the customer form is used to send the reminder. A customer with no usable contact for the chosen channel is skipped and the skip is recorded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:215
msgid "The chatter keeps a full record of every follow-up action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:220
msgid "Follow-ups for several customers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:222
msgid "To act on several customers at once, go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Customers --> Customers`, switch to the list view, and select the customers requiring follow-up (filter by :guilabel:`Overdue Invoices` to narrow the list). Then click :icon:`fa-cog` :guilabel:`(Actions)` and select :guilabel:`Send Payment Reminder`. A review window lists one line per customer with the resolved :guilabel:`Level`; adjust if needed and click :guilabel:`Send`. Each customer receives their full overdue statement. Customers whose overdue balance nets zero or negative are skipped automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:233
msgid "Follow-ups from the overdue invoices list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:235
msgid "You can also start reminders from the invoices list. Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Customers --> Invoices`, filter on :guilabel:`Overdue`, and select the invoices to dun. Then click :icon:`fa-cog` :guilabel:`(Actions)` and select :guilabel:`Send Payment Reminder`. The selected invoices are grouped by customer in the review window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:241
msgid "Unlike the customer-level entry points, a reminder started from the invoices list is **scoped**: it covers only the **selected** invoices (content, attachments, logged record, and interest), not the customer's full statement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:255
msgid "Reminder history on invoices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:257
msgid "On a customer invoice, the :guilabel:`Reminders` smart button and the :guilabel:`Payment Reminders` tab list the reminders that covered the invoice, with their date, channel, level, subject, recipient, and the invoices included."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:264
msgid "Automatic follow-ups"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:266
msgid "A daily scheduled action (:guilabel:`Payment Follow-up: process overdue partners`) processes overdue customers automatically. By design it is **generate-then-review**: it only sends levels that are explicitly flagged :guilabel:`Automatic`. Levels left non-automatic are never sent by the cron and always require a manual review, so no reminder leaves the system unattended unless you opt a level in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:275
msgid "Follow-up letter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:277
msgid "The reminder document is a plain A4 PDF letter listing the customer's overdue invoices, the totals, the optional :ref:`interest and collection-fee block <accounting/follow_up/interest>`, and — in the email — an online **Pay Now** link to the customer portal. The same content is shared between the PDF letter and the reminder email, so both always show the customer the same figures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:292
msgid "Follow-up log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:294
msgid "Every reminder that is sent — and every skipped customer — is written to an append-only audit trail. To review it, go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Reporting --> Payment Follow-up`. Each entry records the date, customer, level, channel (email, SMS, letter, activity, or *skipped*), the invoices covered, and a note. Log entries cannot be edited or deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:309
msgid "Payment risk banner on invoices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:311
msgid "With the *Payment Warning* module installed, a colored banner is displayed at the top of every customer invoice and credit note, summarizing how the customer has been paying. It appears automatically; there is nothing to configure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:315
msgid "The banner states the customer's **average payment delay** over the last twelve months (for example, *This customer pays on average 12 days after the due date*) and lists the customer's **open overdue invoices** with their date and remaining amount. The figures are computed on the commercial partner, so a contact and its parent company are evaluated together, and the invoice being edited is not counted against itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:321
msgid "Its color reflects the risk:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:328
msgid "Shown when"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:329
msgid ":guilabel:`Info` (blue)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:330
msgid "No open overdue invoice, and the average payment delay is 8 days or less (including customers who pay early or on time)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:332
msgid ":guilabel:`Warning` (orange)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:333
msgid "There is at least one open overdue invoice, or the average payment delay is more than 8 days."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:334
msgid ":guilabel:`Danger` (red)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:335
msgid "An invoice is more than 30 days past due, or the average payment delay is more than 30 days."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/follow_up.rst:337
msgid "When there is no payment history and no overdue invoice, no banner is displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:3
msgid "Forecast future bills to pay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:5
msgid "In Odoo, you can manage payments by setting automatic **Payments Terms** and **follow-ups**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:8
msgid "Configuration: payment terms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:10
msgid "In order to track vendor conditions, we use **Payment Terms** in Odoo. They allow keeping track of due dates on invoices. Examples of **Payment Terms** are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:13
msgid "50% within 30 days"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:14
msgid "50% within 45 days"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:16
msgid "To create them, go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Invoicing --> Payment Terms` and click :guilabel:`New` to add new terms, or click existing ones to modify them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:20
msgid ":doc:`../customer_invoices/payment_terms`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:22
msgid "Once **Payment Terms** are defined, you can assign them to your vendor by default. To do so, go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Vendors --> Vendors`, select a vendor, click the :guilabel:`Sales & Purchase` tab, and select a specific **Payment Term** in the :guilabel:`Purchase` section. This way, every time you purchase from this vendor, Odoo automatically proposes the chosen Payment Term."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:28
msgid "If you do not set a specific Payment Term on a vendor, you can still set one on the vendor bill."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:31
msgid "Forecast bills to pay with the aged payable report"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:33
msgid "To track amounts to be paid to the vendors, use the **Aged Payable** report. To access it, go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Reporting --> Dynamic Reports --> Aged Payable`. This report gives you a summary per vendor of the amounts to pay, compared to their due date (the due date being computed on each bill using the terms). This report tells you how much you will have to pay within the following months."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:40
msgid "Select bills to pay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:42
msgid "You can get a list of all your vendor bills by going to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Vendors --> Bills`. To view only the bills that you need to pay, select the :guilabel:`To pay` filter. To view only overdue payments, select the :guilabel:`Overdue` filter instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/accounting/payments/forecast.rst:46
msgid "You can also group bills by their due date by clicking :menuselection:`Group By --> Due Date` and selecting a time period."
