msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:81
msgid "**Accounting board**: the depreciation lines are dated at the **end** of each period (month, quarter, half-year or year) of the fiscal year. The amount of a full period is (gross value − salvage value) × rate × period length / 12. The first line is prorated by the actual calendar days from the activation date to the end of the period; the last line takes the remainder, so the board always ends at zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:88
msgid "Gross value 1,200,000 HUF, salvage value 200,000 HUF, rate 0.20, yearly periods, activated on 15 April 2026: 143,014 HUF in 2026 (261 of 365 days), 200,000 HUF in each of the next four years, and the remaining 56,986 HUF in 2031."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:92
msgid "**TAO board**: yearly lines at the end of the fiscal year. The first year is prorated on a 360-day (12 × 30) basis from the activation date. The board is recomputed together with the accounting board and is never posted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:95
msgid "The :guilabel:`Opening Depreciated Amount` reduces the residual value on both boards; lines that are fully covered by it are not generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:99
msgid "Confirm and depreciate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:101
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Confirm`. For Hungarian assets, a **draft** journal entry *<asset name>: Activation* is created on the journal of the category at the activation date, debiting the asset account and crediting the :guilabel:`Acquisition Account` with the gross value. Review and post it from the :guilabel:`Activation Journal Entry` link. Confirming does not post any depreciation: the due lines are posted by the monthly scheduled action of the asset management or with :menuselection:`Accounting --> Fixed Assets --> Post Depreciation`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:108
msgid "Several draft assets can be confirmed at once from the list view with :menuselection:`Action --> Confirm Assets`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:112
msgid "Do not enable :guilabel:`Auto-Confirm Assets` on categories that use the Hungarian calculation: assets created from vendor bills have no activation date, so the bill could not be posted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:115
msgid "To change the period length of a running asset, use :guilabel:`Modify Depreciation`; the number of depreciations stays computed. The rate itself can only be changed while the asset is in draft."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:119
msgid "Dispose of an asset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:121
msgid "The standard :guilabel:`Sell or Dispose` button is hidden on Hungarian assets. Click :guilabel:`Dispose Asset` (available on running and on fully depreciated assets) and fill in the :guilabel:`Disposal Date`, the :guilabel:`Disposal Type` (:guilabel:`Scrapping`, :guilabel:`Sale` or :guilabel:`Other Withdrawal`) and the :guilabel:`Disposal Reason`. The wizard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:126
msgid "removes the unposted depreciation lines and adds a catch-up line up to the disposal date, with a draft depreciation entry;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:128
msgid "creates the draft entry *<asset name>: Disposal*: accumulated depreciation and :guilabel:`Disposal Expense Account` (net book value) on the debit side, the asset account (gross value) on the credit side;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:131
msgid "closes the asset, fills in the :guilabel:`Disposal` section of the form and shortens the TAO board to the year of the disposal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:134
msgid "Both entries remain in draft for review. In case of a sale, the revenue is invoiced separately with a customer invoice. A disposed asset cannot be reset to draft or confirmed again. The disposal date cannot precede the activation date or the last posted depreciation, and cannot fall into a locked period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:148
msgid "Protocols"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/assets.rst:150
msgid "The :guilabel:`Print` menu of the asset form and list contains four PDF protocols: :guilabel:`Commissioning Protocol` (*üzembe helyezési jegyzőkönyv*), :guilabel:`Asset Increase Protocol` (*állománynövekedési jegyzőkönyv*), :guilabel:`Asset Decrease Protocol` (*állománycsökkenési jegyzőkönyv*) and :guilabel:`Scrapping Protocol` (*selejtezési jegyzőkönyv*). The scrapping protocol shows the net value according to both the Accounting Act and the Corporate Tax Act."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:3
msgid "Cashbook integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:5
msgid "`Cashbook <https://cashbook.hu>`_ is an external Hungarian online service that collects the invoices of a business for bookkeeping and cash-flow follow-up. The :guilabel:`Cashbook integráció` (`eyssen_l10n_hu_cashbook`) module transfers the invoices, credit notes and :doc:`pro-forma invoices <proforma>` of the company to Cashbook automatically, as structured data together with the PDF, and re-sends an invoice with its payment data whenever a payment is reconciled with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:12
msgid "This integration is not related to the :doc:`cash register <../../accounting/bank/cash_register>` (*házipénztár*) feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:14
msgid "The module requires `eyssen_l10n_hu` and `eyssen_l10n_hu_proforma`. Its labels are displayed in Hungarian in the current module version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:20
msgid "Request an API key from Cashbook, then go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings`, section :guilabel:`Cashbook adatszolgáltatás` (the same fields are available in the :guilabel:`CashBook adatszolgáltatás` tab of the company form):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:24
msgid "tick :guilabel:`Cashbook adatszolgáltatás`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:25
msgid ":guilabel:`Üzemmód`: :guilabel:`Teszt üzemmód` (test system, the default) or :guilabel:`Éles adatszolgáltatás` (production);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:27
msgid ":guilabel:`Ne küldjük be a Cashbook-nak a számlákat. KIZÁRÓLAG TESZTELÉSRE!`: suspends the transfer, for testing;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:29
msgid ":guilabel:`Cashbook kulcs`: the API key."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:39
msgid "At installation, a to-do activity *Cashbook adatszolgáltatáshoz be kell állítani!* is created on every company. A copied (neutralized) database is switched to test mode with the transfer disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:43
msgid "Enter the API key right after installing the module. In the current module version, confirming a pro-forma invoice and reconciling a payment fail while the key is empty, even if the :guilabel:`Cashbook adatszolgáltatás` option is not ticked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:47
msgid "To exclude a whole journal (for example, a journal of invoices issued in another system), open it in :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>` and tick :guilabel:`Nem kell átadni a Cashbook-nak!` in the :guilabel:`Hungarian Invoicing` section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:52
msgid "Transfer and follow-up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:54
msgid "Posted customer invoices, vendor bills and credit notes, as well as confirmed pro-forma invoices, are queued when they are confirmed; a background job sends them about a minute later and retries every five minutes. The PDF sent is the main attachment of the document, or the printed invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/cashbook.rst:58
msgid "The :guilabel:`CashBook` tab of the invoice and of the pro-forma invoice shows the :guilabel:`Cashbook státusz`, which is also available as a column in the invoice, credit note and pro-forma lists: *Beküldés folyamatban* (queued), *Beküldve* (sent), *Sikeresen feldolgozva* (processed), or the error reported by Cashbook (for example, unreadable data, missing PDF, unknown tax number, or missing permission for vendor bills). In :ref:`developer mode <developer-mode>`, the tab contains the buttons :guilabel:`Beküldés a CashBook-ba`, :guilabel:`Azonnali beküldés a CashBook-ba` and :guilabel:`Státusz ellenőrzés` for administrators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:3
msgid "VAT return with NAV eÁFA (eVAT M2M)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:5
msgid "The :guilabel:`Hungary - eVAT (eÁFA M2M) VAT Return` (`l10n_hu_evat`) module files the Hungarian VAT return through the *eÁFA* machine-to-machine interface of NAV instead of an ÁNYK form. Odoo builds the VAT **analytics** of the period from the posted journal entries (one line per source document, classified with the *standard tax codes* of NAV), validates them with the rules and the XML schema published by NAV, uploads them in the background, follows the processing at NAV, and finally an approver submits the legally binding return. Self-revisions and corrections of submitted returns are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:14
msgid "The module requires `eyssen_l10n_hu` and uses the technical user of the :doc:`NAV Online Számla reporting <nav_online_invoice>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:16
msgid "Returns can only be generated for companies whose currency is HUF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:17
msgid "The module is independent of the :doc:`ÁNYK form packages <vat_return>`; use one of the two methods for a given period. The domestic recapitulative M sheets and the EC recapitulative statement (`A60`) are not part of this module: the partner-level data travel in the analytics lines, and the recapitulative statement is prepared with the ÁNYK form package."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:28
msgid "Two access rights are available in the :guilabel:`Hungarian eVAT` category of the user form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:30
msgid ":guilabel:`eVAT User`: create, generate, validate and upload returns, reopen aborted returns, and fetch the NAV documents;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:32
msgid ":guilabel:`eVAT Approve`: everything above, plus delete draft returns and **submit** the return to NAV. The administrator receives this right at installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:35
msgid "The configuration menus require the :guilabel:`Administrator` accounting access right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:38
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/nav_online_invoice.rst:25
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/proforma.rst:30
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:40
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Configuration --> Settings`, section :guilabel:`Hungarian eVAT`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:42
msgid ":guilabel:`eVAT M2M Enabled`: enables the interface for the company;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:43
msgid ":guilabel:`eVAT Software ID`: the 18-character identifier (digits and capital letters) of the software, pre-filled;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:45
msgid ":guilabel:`NAV Mode`: displays the :guilabel:`Test`/:guilabel:`Production` mode selected in the :ref:`NAV Data Reporting settings <localizations/hungary/nav-settings>`; the matching user name, password and signing key of those settings are used;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:48
msgid ":guilabel:`eVAT VPID`: the 12-digit customs identifier, needed only if a tax account transfer line credits a customs-related tax type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:60
msgid "Standard tax codes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:62
msgid "Every analytics line carries a NAV *standard tax code*, which describes the type of the transaction and its VAT rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:65
msgid ":menuselection:`Accounting --> eVAT --> Configuration --> Standard Tax Codes` contains the catalogue published by NAV. :guilabel:`Sync from NAV` downloads new codes and closes expired ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:67
msgid "On each tax, set the default code in the :guilabel:`eVAT` tab, field :guilabel:`eVAT Standard Tax Code`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:69
msgid ":menuselection:`Accounting --> eVAT --> Configuration --> Mapping Rules` handles the exceptions. A rule has :guilabel:`Conditions` (:guilabel:`Taxes`, :guilabel:`Move Types`, :guilabel:`Partner Status`, :guilabel:`Fiscal Positions`, :guilabel:`Product Categories`, :guilabel:`Products`) and a :guilabel:`Result`: the :guilabel:`eVAT Standard Tax Code` and the :guilabel:`Taxpoint Strategy` (:guilabel:`Default`, :guilabel:`Delivery date`, :guilabel:`Accounting date` or :guilabel:`Period end`). The first matching rule wins; if no rule matches, the default code of the tax is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:76
msgid "A document whose tax has neither a rule nor a default code is skipped and reported on the :guilabel:`Validation` tab of the return (code `GEN0001`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:80
msgid "Other tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:82
msgid ":guilabel:`MNB Base Rates`: the central bank base rate series used to compute the self-revision surcharge. The historical rates are preloaded; **add a new row whenever the base rate changes**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:84
msgid ":guilabel:`VTSZ Tariff Mapping`: maps the VTSZ prefixes of domestic reverse-charge goods (agricultural products, steel, gas) to the product category and unit of measure required on sheets `07` and `08`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:91
msgid "Prepare and file a return"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:93
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Accounting --> eVAT --> Declarations` and click :guilabel:`New`. Set the :guilabel:`Period Start`, the :guilabel:`Period End` and the :guilabel:`Frequency` (:guilabel:`Monthly`, :guilabel:`Quarterly` or :guilabel:`Annual`), then follow the steps below. The status bar shows the main steps: :guilabel:`Draft`, :guilabel:`Generated`, :guilabel:`Finished` and :guilabel:`Submitted`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:99
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Generate`. The analytics lines are built from the posted entries of the period (taxes due on payment are included by payment date), the summary is computed, the local validation runs and the reverse-charge sheets `07`/`08` are filled in. :guilabel:`Reset to Draft` discards the generated data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:103
msgid "Review the tabs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:105
msgid ":guilabel:`Lines`: the analytics lines with their source document, taxpoint date and partner;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:106
msgid ":guilabel:`Summary`: payable, deductible, reclaimed and transferable tax in thousand HUF. Tick :guilabel:`Lapsed Residual Tax` if the amount carried forward from the previous period can no longer be used;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:109
msgid ":guilabel:`Statements`: the :guilabel:`Return Decision` (:guilabel:`No return`, :guilabel:`Full return` or :guilabel:`Tax account transfer`), the :guilabel:`Refund Entitlement Code` and the procedure indicators of the return. Click :guilabel:`Compute Summary` after changing them;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:112
msgid ":guilabel:`Transfer (170)`: the transfer request lines, if the return decision is a tax account transfer;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:114
msgid ":guilabel:`Reverse charge (07/08)`: the domestic reverse-charge sheets, which can be regenerated with :guilabel:`Regenerate 07/08 Sheets`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:116
msgid ":guilabel:`Validation`: the messages of the local check (:guilabel:`Critical`, :guilabel:`Error`, :guilabel:`Warning`, :guilabel:`Info`). Correct the source documents or the tax code mapping, and click :guilabel:`Generate` again after a :guilabel:`Reset to Draft`. :guilabel:`Validate` reruns the check at any time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:121
msgid "Optionally, click :guilabel:`Export XML` to download the analytics file (`EVAT_<start>_<end>_v<version>.xml`) for review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:123
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Upload to NAV`. The return must be free of local validation errors. The status changes to :guilabel:`Uploading`, and a background job uploads the data about a minute later. If the upload fails, the return goes back to :guilabel:`Generated` and the reason is shown in the :guilabel:`Error Note` of the :guilabel:`NAV` tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:127
msgid "NAV processes the upload. A scheduled action checks the status every five minutes (:guilabel:`Received` → :guilabel:`Processing` → :guilabel:`BEVFELD Check` → :guilabel:`Finished`); :guilabel:`Check Status Now` checks it on demand. The messages of NAV are added to the :guilabel:`Validation` tab. If NAV rejects the data, the status becomes :guilabel:`Aborted`: click :guilabel:`Reopen`, correct the problem and upload again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:132
msgid "When the status is :guilabel:`Finished`, every user with the :guilabel:`eVAT Approve` right receives a to-do activity *Submit eVAT declaration to NAV*. The :guilabel:`Submission Deadline` on the :guilabel:`NAV` tab shows until when the processed data is kept by NAV (30 days); after that the upload must be repeated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:136
msgid "An approver clicks :guilabel:`Submit to NAV`. The dialog lists the high-priority warnings of NAV, which must be acknowledged with :guilabel:`I acknowledge the warnings above`, and reminds that *submitting is the legally binding filing of the VAT return with NAV* and cannot be undone. After the confirmation the status is :guilabel:`Submitted` and the return document received from NAV is attached."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:151
msgid "The taxpoint date of a document is its fulfillment date, unless a mapping rule sets another strategy. It can be overridden on the :guilabel:`eVAT` tab of the invoice (:guilabel:`eVAT Taxpoint Date`). The same tab lists the returns that contain the invoice, and :guilabel:`Query NAV Tax Codes` shows the codes NAV suggests for a posted invoice (for information only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:156
msgid "Vendor bills are identified by their :guilabel:`Bill Reference`; bills without a reference are skipped with a validation message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:160
msgid "Reconcile with the NAV data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:162
msgid "On the :guilabel:`NAV Documents` tab, click :guilabel:`Fetch NAV Documents` to download the invoice data, cash register summaries and customs declarations that NAV holds for the period. The :guilabel:`Reconciliation Summary` and the :guilabel:`NAV Match` badge of the lines show which documents are :guilabel:`Matched` and which are :guilabel:`Missing in Odoo`, for example vendor bills that were not recorded yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:169
msgid "Self-revision and correction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:171
msgid "On a :guilabel:`Submitted` return, click :guilabel:`Self-check` (*önellenőrzés*) or :guilabel:`Correction` to create the next version for the same period, then generate, upload and submit it like a base return. The :guilabel:`Changes` tab compares it with the original return (summary differences and added, removed and changed lines)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:176
msgid "For a self-revision, the :guilabel:`Self-check (04)` tab contains the self-revision surcharge (*önellenőrzési pótlék*). Select the :guilabel:`Non-standard Calculation Reason` if one applies, and click :guilabel:`Compute Allowance`: the surcharge is computed from the MNB base rate, from the day after the original deadline, with a 50% increase for a repeated self-revision. If the surcharge was computed on an earlier day than the submission, the submit dialog asks to acknowledge it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:183
msgid "Scheduled actions and limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:185
msgid "Two scheduled actions are created: *eVAT: poll NAV processing status* (every 5 minutes) and *eVAT: remove finished one-shot upload jobs* (hourly)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/evat.rst:188
msgid "The following are not supported in the current module version: the sheets for animal disease deferment, bad debt, chassis numbers and new means of transport; attachments to the return; and the automatic handling of lapsed residual tax. There is no PDF print of the return."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:3
msgid "Hungarian invoicing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:5
msgid "The `eyssen_l10n_hu` module adapts customer invoices and vendor bills to the Hungarian VAT Act. The features below are available for companies whose fiscal country is Hungary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:11
#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:88
msgid "Fulfillment date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:13
msgid "The :guilabel:`Fulfillment Date` (*teljesítés időpontja*) is displayed below the :guilabel:`Invoice Date` on customer invoices, vendor bills and credit notes, and the :guilabel:`Accounting Date` is always visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:17
msgid "On customer invoices, the accounting date must be equal to the fulfillment date. If they differ, the red banner *The Accounting Date is not the same as the Fulfillment Date!* is displayed and the invoice cannot be confirmed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:20
msgid "If the fulfillment date is empty when :guilabel:`Confirm` is clicked, a :guilabel:`Fulfillment Date` dialog asks whether today can be used: :guilabel:`Yes, use today` or :guilabel:`No, keep editing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:23
msgid "When a sales order with *delivered quantities* products is invoiced, the accounting and fulfillment dates are set to the date of the latest delivery. With the `eyssen_l10n_hu_sale_stock_delivery_date` module, this also works together with the standard *effective date* logic of the Inventory app; the dates of posted invoices are never recomputed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:27
msgid "Corrective invoices and credit notes always inherit the fulfillment date and the accounting date of the original invoice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:29
msgid "The exchange rate of foreign-currency invoices is the rate of the fulfillment date (today's rate if the fulfillment date is in the future). The printed invoice repeats the VAT summary in HUF and shows the exchange rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:33
msgid "A yellow banner *The invoice is not made out to the company, but to a contact or delivery address!* warns when the selected customer is a child contact of a company."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:47
msgid "Checks at confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:49
msgid "A **customer invoice** or credit note can only be confirmed if"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/finance/fiscal_localizations/hungary/invoicing.rst:51
msgid "the customer has a country, ZIP code, city and street;"
msgstr ""

